{
  "description": "Ownership label vectors (registry/ownership.json, docs/images-and-ownership.md). The client profile doing the operation is `profile`. ownership_cases: labels read by inspect from an existing container, volume or network; owned=true only if managed=true and profile equals the current profile (operation_id is not checked). An unowned resource is skipped by list/cleanup and never changed (FOREIGN_RESOURCE when an operation needed to change it). caller_label_cases: extra labels requested by a caller for a new resource; refused if a key is in the reserved namespace or a key or value leaves the label charset. adoption_cases: SEC-m5, an existing labelled resource is reused only if it is in the journal and inspect shows an allowlisted image without host mounts, privileged or the Docker socket.",
  "profile": "default",
